Position overview 
 We are looking for a Senior C++ Software Engineer to join our Randstad Digital Romania team in Bucharest for a specialized project. Our partner is a major player in railway infrastructure, developing advanced signaling, traffic management, and digital train control systems.
 In this role, you will be responsible for designing, coding, and qualifying safe software components in line with functional specifications for safety-critical products where code quality directly impacts public safety within the field of railway control and safety technology.
 Responsibilities 
Object-oriented (C++) design and implementation according to requirements and interface specifications, ensuring compliance with CENELEC standards;
Create and review technical documentation, including requirement specifications, detailed design, architecture documents, and test specifications;
Create, manage, and maintain automated unit tests, and document the results;
Perform requirements tracing from functional specifications down to the code level;
Conduct defect analysis, debugging, and software correction;
Perform requirements analysis using DOORS and object-oriented design in UML;
Implement code in C++ adhering strictly to MISRA C++ guidelines;
Actively participate and contribute within an Agile development process.
 Requirements 
Minimum of 5 years of professional experience in C++ software development;
Strong fundamental understanding of software design patterns, principles, and component-oriented design practices;
Expertise in development processes for safety-critical software and implementation of C++ code in compliance with MISRA C++ guidelines;
Ability to create and review technical documentation (requirement specifications, detailed design, architecture documents, test specifications) and perform object-oriented design in UML;
Hands-on creation and maintenance of automated unit tests, documenting test results, and tracing requirements from functional specifications down to code;
Practical working knowledge of Linux operating systems and experience working within Agile software development processes;
Bachelor's or Master's Degree in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, Electrical Engineering, or a comparable technical field;
Excellent communication skills and a team-oriented mindset;
Highly self-organized and capable of working autonomously;
Agile mindset, contributing positively to an open-minded team spirit;
Strong proficiency in English language (fluent, spoken and written).
 Nice to have 
Experience in embedded development using C/C++;
Additional knowledge of relevant CENELEC norms.;
Knowledge of Linux operating systems and familiarity with other programming languages;
Requirements Analysis in DOORS: Experience analyzing requirements and managing specifications using IBM DOORS;
Multinational Safety-Critical Domain Experience: Prior background working on complex railway control or similar high-safety critical products.
 Benefits 
Attractive salary package according to your experience and seniority bonus;
The 13th salary depending on company’s performance;
Bonus for internal recommendations;
Meal tickets;
Private health insurance, including dental services and psychological consultations;
Flexible working hours (core-hours system);
Access to over 600 sports centers in the 7Card network;
Online language courses: English and French;
Access to the e-learning platform;
Access to technical training programs / workshops, as well as other technical events (both as a participant and as a speaker);
Development opportunities through involvement in internship & mentoring programs;
Access to soft-skills programs and workshops;
Access to various internal events and team-buildings;
Access to international opportunities for career development with challenging and exciting projects in a dynamic international working environment;
Paid days off offered for involvement in volunteering activities and for bank holidays occasion.
 Kindly note that only suitable candidates will be contacted. 
